# GitKraken commit style (persistent)

This file was written by `/gitkraken-commit-message` when you chose **this commit and onward**.

When drafting or creating commits in this repo:

- Follow `.cursor/skills/gitkraken-commit-message/references/style.md`.
- Do not use Conventional Commits prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`).
- Do not ask whether to use that style. It stays on until this rule is removed.

**To stop and get the once/onward prompt again:** delete this file (`.cursor/rules/gitkraken-commit-style.mdc`). Nothing else to undo.
